      "answer": "The **lost-in-the-middle effect** is the tendency of language models to use relevant information in long input contexts less effectively when that information appears in the middle. Performance is typically highest when the relevant information is near the **beginning** or **end** of the context\u2014reflecting primacy and recency biases\u2014and drops substantially when it is located in the middle [1][3][5].\n\nIt has been observed in tasks such as multi-document question answering and key-value retrieval, including in models designed for long contexts [1].",
